<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>os-device-onboarding – package repository</title>
<style>
  :root { --bg:#fbfbfa; --fg:#1d1d1b; --muted:#66645e; --line:#e3e1db; --code:#f1efea; --accent:#d94f00; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root { --bg:#161615; --fg:#ecebe7; --muted:#a3a19a; --line:#34332f; --code:#22211f; --accent:#ff7a2e; }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--fg);
         font:16px/1.6 system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif; }
  main { max-width:760px; margin:0 auto; padding:48px 16px 64px; }
  h1 { font-size:1.9rem; line-height:1.2; margin:0 0 4px; }
  h2 { font-size:1.15rem; margin:40px 0 8px; padding-top:16px; border-top:1px solid var(--line); }
  .sub { color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 24px; }
  .badge { display:inline-block; font-size:.85rem; padding:2px 10px; border:1px solid var(--line);
           border-radius:999px; color:var(--muted); margin-right:6px; }
  pre { background:var(--code); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:8px; padding:14px 16px;
        overflow-x:auto; font:14px/1.5 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace; }
  code { font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace; font-size:.92em; }
  a { color:var(--accent); }
  ol li { margin-bottom:6px; }
  .note { color:var(--muted); font-size:.95rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>os-device-onboarding</h1>
  <p class="sub">OPNsense plugin: time-limited internet access for new devices, permanent access via aliases.</p>
  <p><span class="badge">version %%VERSION%%</span><span class="badge">built %%DATE%%</span><span class="badge">signed repository</span></p>

  <p>This is a <code>pkg(8)</code> repository for the plugin. After adding it once, the plugin can be
  installed and updated from the OPNsense GUI like any other plugin.
  Source code and documentation: <a href="https://github.com/alexsxb/OPNsense-Device-Onboarding">GitHub</a>.</p>

  <h2>1. Add the repository (once)</h2>
  <p>On the OPNsense console or via SSH, as root:</p>
<pre>mkdir -p /usr/local/etc/pkg/keys
fetch -o /usr/local/etc/pkg/keys/device-onboarding.pub \
  https://alexsxb.github.io/OPNsense-Device-Onboarding/device-onboarding.pub
fetch -o /usr/local/etc/pkg/repos/device-onboarding.conf \
  https://alexsxb.github.io/OPNsense-Device-Onboarding/device-onboarding.conf
pkg update -r device-onboarding</pre>

  <h2>2. Install</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>System → Firmware → Plugins</strong>, search for <code>os-device-onboarding</code>, click <strong>+</strong>.<br>
        Or on the console: <code>pkg install os-device-onboarding</code></li>
    <li>Open <strong>Services → Device Onboarding</strong>, select interface and DHCP pool, enable, <em>Apply</em>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="note">Updates appear in <em>System → Firmware → Updates</em> together with the OPNsense updates.</p>

  <h2>Remove the repository</h2>
<pre>pkg delete os-device-onboarding      # optional: remove the plugin
rm /usr/local/etc/pkg/repos/device-onboarding.conf \
   /usr/local/etc/pkg/keys/device-onboarding.pub</pre>

  <h2>Verification</h2>
  <p class="note">The repository catalogue is signed. <code>pkg</code> verifies it with the public key
  <a href="device-onboarding.pub">device-onboarding.pub</a>; packages are checked against the catalogue checksums.
  Requires Dnsmasq as DHCP server. Community software, not supported by the OPNsense project.</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
